  hypothesis
    defined-by concept
    role proof_step_kind
    precondition "a proof or a proof plan states what it assumes before it derives anything"
    effect "the step is presented as an assumption the later steps build on"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "Assume for contradiction that only finitely many primes exist."
    grounding "data/seed/proof-library.lino"
  axiom
    defined-by concept
    role proof_step_kind
    precondition "a proof fixes the formal system it reasons inside"
    effect "the step is presented as an accepted starting point that is not itself proved"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "Take the axiom set N of Newtonian mechanics."
    grounding "data/seed/proof-library.lino"
  inference
    defined-by concept
    role proof_step_kind
    precondition "earlier steps of a proof license a new statement"
    effect "the step is presented as derived from the steps before it"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "Hence q is a prime not in the list."
    grounding "data/seed/proof-library.lino"
  sub_proof
    defined-by concept
    role proof_step_kind
    precondition "a proof needs an auxiliary argument inside its main line"
    effect "the step is presented as a nested argument whose result the main proof uses"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "A side note marks the limit of the reduction before the conclusion."
    grounding "data/seed/proof-library.lino"
  conclusion
    defined-by concept
    role proof_step_kind
    precondition "the steps of a proof or a plan reach their goal"
    effect "the step states what has been established or what the plan will establish"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "The assumption fails, so there are infinitely many primes."
    grounding "data/seed/proof-library.lino"
  known_theorem
    defined-by method
    role proof_method
    precondition "a claim names a classical result the proof library holds"
    effect "the claim is discharged by restating the library's textbook proof"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "the Pythagorean theorem proved through the similar triangles cut by the altitude"
    grounding "data/seed/proof-library.lino"
  induction
    defined-by method
    role proof_method
    precondition "a claim ranges over the natural numbers or another well-founded order"
    effect "the claim is proved for a base case and carried from each case to the next"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "Fermat's little theorem proved by induction on a"
    grounding "data/seed/proof-library.lino"
  axiom_reduction
    defined-by method
    role proof_method
    precondition "a claim only becomes checkable inside a chosen axiom set"
    effect "the claim is restated inside that axiom set and reduced to statements the set decides"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "Laplacian determinism reduced to existence and uniqueness of solutions of an ODE"
    grounding "data/seed/proof-library.lino"
